IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition,
-- informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2026.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill and
-- nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. SECTION 15 ONLY, subsections (1) to (6) -- when money may come out of
-- the Fund. The Act is about 911,000 characters across 8 Parts and more than a
-- hundred sections; this is a few pages of it. Contributions (ss 7-9D), the
-- subsidiary accounts (s 13), housing and investment charges, nominations
-- (s 25), the Retirement Sum Scheme machinery in s 15AA and the whole of
-- Parts 3A onwards are NOT encoded.
--
-- Everything prescribed -- the retirement sum itself, the classes of person
-- prescribed as "applicable", the conditions the Board may impose -- is a fact
-- supplied. Those carry most of the practical content, and the regulations were
-- not retrieved.

§ `Central Provident Fund Act 1953 -- section 15`

§§ `2 -- "applicable person"`

-- s 2: "'applicable person' means -- (a) a citizen or permanent resident of
-- Singapore; or (b) for the purposes of a provision of this Act ..., any other
-- person of a class prescribed by regulations made under section 77(1) for the
-- purposes of that provision."
--
-- The second limb is prescribed and not retrieved, so it arrives as a fact.
DECLARE Member HAS
    `name`                                      IS A STRING
    `a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a class prescribed under section 77(1) as an applicable person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has attained the age of 55 years`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 15(3): a further withdrawal arises on each anniversary of the date of
    -- birth AFTER a withdrawal made on the 55 ground. Whether an anniversary
    -- has come round is a date question this toolchain cannot compute, so it is
    -- a fact; what the encoding decides is whether the entitlement exists.
    `has already withdrawn on the ground of having attained 55` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an anniversary of the date of birth has since passed, or the Minister has directed another period` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 15(6): the retirement sum set-aside.
    `the sum standing to the member's credit`    IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed retirement sum applicable to the member` IS A NUMBER
    `a reserved amount standing to the member's credit` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is an applicable person` IF
        `the member`'s `a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    OR  `the member`'s `of a class prescribed under section 77(1) as an applicable person`

§§ `15(1) -- nothing comes out without the Board`

-- s 15(1): "NO sum of money standing to the credit of a member of the Fund may
-- be withdrawn from the Fund EXCEPT WITH THE AUTHORITY OF THE BOARD."
--
-- A flat prohibition, and the premise of everything below: the subsections that
-- follow create entitlements, and an entitlement is still not a withdrawal
-- until the Board authorises it.
GIVEN `the Board has given its authority under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `money may lawfully be withdrawn` IF
    `the Board has given its authority under section 15(1)`

§§ `15(2) -- the two grounds of entitlement`

-- s 15(2): "Subject to section 16, a member of the Fund is entitled to withdraw
-- the sum standing to the credit of the member in the Fund at any time after
-- the Board is satisfied that the member -- (a) has attained the age of
-- 55 years; or (b) IS NOT AN APPLICABLE PERSON."
--
-- Paragraphs (c) to (g) were repealed between 2021 and 2024, so what is left is
-- a two-way choice: reach 55, or stop being a citizen or permanent resident.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(a)` IF
    `the member`'s `has attained the age of 55 years`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(b)` IF
    NOT `the member is an applicable person` `the member`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)` IF
        `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(a)` `the member`
    OR  `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(b)` `the member`

§§ `15(3) -- the annual further withdrawal`

-- s 15(3): "Subject to subsection (6) and section 16, a member of the Fund who
-- has withdrawn any money from the Fund ON THE GROUND THAT HE OR SHE HAS
-- ATTAINED 55 YEARS OF AGE is entitled to make a further withdrawal of the sum
-- standing to his or her credit in the Fund on or after EACH SUBSEQUENT
-- ANNIVERSARY of his or her date of birth or such other period as the Minister
-- may direct."
--
-- Note which ground it attaches to. A member who withdrew under (2)(b),
-- because they ceased to be a citizen or permanent resident, is not within
-- s 15(3) at all -- see the note in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to a further withdrawal under section 15(3)` IF
        `the member`'s `has already withdrawn on the ground of having attained 55`
    AND `the member`'s `an anniversary of the date of birth has since passed, or the Minister has directed another period`

§§ `15(6) -- the retirement sum must be set aside first`

-- s 15(6): "where a member of the Fund is entitled under subsection (2)(a)
-- or (3), or is allowed under subsection (4), to withdraw the sum standing to
-- the member's credit in the Fund, at the time of the withdrawal ... (a) such
-- retirement sum applicable to the member as may be prescribed must be set
-- aside or topped-up -- (i) by the member; or (ii) from the sum standing to the
-- member's credit in the Fund, AFTER EXCLUDING ANY RESERVED AMOUNT ..."
--
-- The set-aside attaches to (2)(a), (3) and (4). It does NOT attach to (2)(b).
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retirement sum must be set aside` IF
        `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(a)` `the member`
    OR  `the member is entitled to a further withdrawal under section 15(3)` `the member`

-- What is actually available once the retirement sum is set aside out of the
-- credit, the reserved amount having been excluded from the sum it is taken
-- from.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the sum available to set the retirement sum aside from` IS
    `the member`'s `the sum standing to the member's credit`
        MINUS `the member`'s `a reserved amount standing to the member's credit`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the credit is enough to set aside the retirement sum` IF
    `the sum available to set the retirement sum aside from` `the member`
        AT LEAST `the member`'s `the prescribed retirement sum applicable to the member`

-- The amount a member entitled under (2)(a) or (3) can actually take out: what
-- is left after the retirement sum is set aside. Where the credit will not
-- cover the retirement sum, nothing is withdrawable and the whole credit is set
-- aside -- hence the floor at nought rather than a negative figure.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount withdrawable after the set-aside` IS
    IF   `the credit is enough to set aside the retirement sum` `the member`
    THEN `the sum available to set the retirement sum aside from` `the member`
             MINUS `the member`'s `the prescribed retirement sum applicable to the member`
    ELSE 0

-- The whole of s 15 as one question, for a member who is not relying on the
-- Board's discretion under (4). The Board's authority under (1) is required on
-- top of any entitlement.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `the Board has given its authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount this member may withdraw` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Board has given its authority` THEN 0
        IF `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(b)` `the member`
            THEN `the member`'s `the sum standing to the member's credit`
        IF `the retirement sum must be set aside` `the member`
            THEN `the amount withdrawable after the set-aside` `the member`
        OTHERWISE 0
